
1582 Problem:-
Given an m x n binary matrix mat, return the number of special positions in mat.
A position (i, j) is called special if mat[i][j] == 1 and all other elements in row i and column j are 0 (rows and columns are 0-indexed).

Example 1:
Input: mat = [[1,0,0],[0,0,1],[1,0,0]]
Output: 1
Explanation: (1, 2) is a special position because mat[1][2] == 1 and all other elements in row 1 and column 2 are 0.

Example 2:
Input: mat = [[1,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,1]]
Output: 3
Explanation: (0, 0), (1, 1) and (2, 2) are special positions.
 
Constraints:
m == mat.length
n == mat[i].length
1 <= m, n <= 100
mat[i][j] is either 0 or 1.

================================================================================================================================================================

Solution:-
Intuition:-
A position (i, j) is special if:
mat[i][j] == 1
It is the only 1 in its row
It is the only 1 in its column
Instead of checking the entire row and column every time (which would be inefficient), we can precompute how many 1s each row and column contains.
If a cell is 1 and both its row count and column count equal 1, then it must be special.

Approach:-
Create two arrays:
row[i] → count of 1s in row i
col[j] → count of 1s in column j
First pass:
Traverse matrix
Count 1s for every row and column
Second pass:
If mat[i][j] == 1
AND row[i] == 1
AND col[j] == 1
Increase answer

Complexity:-
Time complexity:O(m × n)
Space complexity:O(m + n)

Code:-
class Solution {
    public int numSpecial(int[][] mat) {
        int m = mat.length, n = mat[0].length;
        int[] row = new int[m];
        int[] col = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (mat[i][j] == 1) {
                    row[i]++;
                    col[j]++;
                }
            }
        }

        int ans = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (mat[i][j] == 1 && row[i] == 1 && col[j] == 1) {
                    ans++;
                }
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
